      "slug": "gram:gp-118",
      "variants": [],
      "steps_unavailable": "Discontinuous two-site pattern. しか attaches to a noun or a quantity, but the obligatory negation lands on a DIFFERENT word, the predicate verb (水しか飲まない, 一人しか来なかった). The op set only appends to one base, so no sequence can force the nai-form onto the separate predicate. Encoding just the noun side would license the ungrammatical 千円しかある, which the record own nuance field flags as wrong.",
      "nuance_tags": ["emphasis"],
      "usage_contexts": ["spoken", "written"]
    },
